    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "All tests pass and the build is green.\n\n## Summary\n\nThe task required all rejection responses (400, 409, 429) to return an RFC7807 `application/problem+json` body with `type`, `title`, `status`, and `detail`.\n\n**Starting state:** The 400 rejections already flowed through `ExceptionControllerAdvice`, which builds a Spring `ProblemDetail` (RFC7807). But the 429 and 409 rejections in `OwnerRestControllerV1.addOwner` returned bodyless `ResponseEntity<>(HttpStatus.\u2026)`. Because the controller implements the generated `OwnersApi` interface (return type pinned to `ResponseEntity<OwnerDto>`), a bare status couldn't carry a `ProblemDetail` body directly \u2014 so the idiomatic Spring fix is to throw exceptions and handle them in the advice.\n\n**Changes:**\n- Added three exceptions in `util/`: `RegistrationRateLimitException` (429), `DuplicateOwnerException` (409, identity-key conflict), `CityCapacityException` (409, city-at-capacity) \u2014 matching the existing exception convention.\n- `OwnerRestControllerV1`: replaced the three bodyless `ResponseEntity` returns with `throw`s of these exceptions.\n- `ExceptionControllerAdvice`: added three `@ExceptionHandler` methods that reuse the existing `detailBuild(...)` helper to emit a `ProblemDetail` with the same 429/409 HTTP status codes \u2014 unchanged status codes, now with full problem+json bodies (`type`, `title`, `status`, `detail`).\n\nEach handler returns `ResponseEntity<ProblemDetail>`, which Spring serializes as `application/problem+json` \u2014 identical to the already-passing 400 path.\n\n**Verification:** `./mvnw test` \u2192 `BUILD SUCCESS`, `Tests run: 1, Failures: 0, Errors: 0` (including the `coreRejectionIsProblemJson` acceptance test asserting the content type and `$.status`).",
